  "cause": "The harness did not malfunction: its refusal \"no file ... in task\" was true. The model (claude-haiku-4-5) called workspace.read on paths that are not files of the task workspace. In t-2026-09-25-0017 it read \"evaluation.procedure\", which is a field of the reasoning state (/evaluation), not a file. Steps 9, 11 and 15 were refused for it. In t-2026-09-25-0026 it read manifest.json at step 9, which succeeded. It then guessed \"results/step-009-procedure-submit.json\", which does not exist, and sent the identical call 16 times (steps 10 to 25) until the task failed on iterations. The refusal names the missing file but does not list the files that exist, and the harness does not stop an identical repeat. That let the model loop, but the origin is a model that confuses state fields with workspace files and invents file names. The two tasks ran under different fingerprints (433bbb9878a7 and e189827ff35b), so a prompt change is not the cause.",
